    {
      "id": 18,
      "title": "Price source share (which table produced the price)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Share of AI price lookups by the table that produced the price: catalog is the shipped model catalog, rate_card and config are operator-supplied, and fallback is the pessimistic default of $5 per million tokens in and $5 per million out, applied when nothing else priced the model. That default is usually well above a real price, so a rising fallback share normally overstates spend and trips budget caps and the price ceiling early; on a genuinely expensive model it understates. Counted per price lookup and not per request, so one request can contribute several samples. When fallback climbs, add the missing model to the catalog or to a rate card. The family carries only the source label, so this panel is fleet-wide, the Tenant and Credential dropdowns do not apply to it, and it cannot say which model fell back. The red not reported series sits at 1 when no AI request has ever been priced on this instance, which is not the same as a zero fallback share. Runbook: docs/operator-runbook.md.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "not reported"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "short"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (source) (rate(sbproxy_ai_price_source_total[5m])) / ignoring(source) group_left sum(rate(sbproxy_ai_price_source_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{source}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "absent(sbproxy_ai_price_source_total)",
          "legendFormat": "not reported",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "title": "Price ceiling outcomes",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 36
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Rate of price-ceiling guard outcomes. candidate_excluded is a routing candidate dropped for being priced over the ceiling, counted per candidate, so one request can contribute several. refused is a request where every candidate was over the ceiling and the caller was answered 402. invalid_header is an unparseable x-sbproxy-max-price and is a client integration bug, not a pricing problem. unsupported_surface is a header ceiling set on a surface with no pre-dispatch cost estimate; only chat completions, messages, and responses can enforce one. Steady exclusions with no refusals is the healthy shape. Refusals climbing means the ceiling now sits below the cheapest available candidate, so raise the ceiling or add a cheaper model to the route. The family carries only the outcome label, so this panel is fleet-wide and the Tenant and Credential dropdowns do not apply. The red not reported series sits at 1 when no price ceiling has ever been evaluated on this instance. Runbook: docs/operator-runbook.md.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "not reported"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "short"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(sbproxy_ai_price_ceiling_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "absent(sbproxy_ai_price_ceiling_total)",
          "legendFormat": "not reported",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "title": "Token estimate error by model (p05 and p95)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 44
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Relative error of the pre-request token estimate against the upstream usage.prompt_tokens, per model, sign preserved as (actual - estimated) / actual. Positive means the estimator under-reserved and the request cost more than it debited from the budget. Negative means it over-reserved, which over-debits the budget and holds rate-limit headroom the request never used. p95 tracks the under-reserving tail and p05 the over-reserving one, because a p95 near zero says nothing about an estimator that is systematically too high. The buckets cut at +/- 0.10, so either line sitting outside that band means headroom and ceiling decisions are being made on a bad number; refresh the tokenizer for that model. This is recorded only on a reconciled rate-limit admission, which requires the model to hold an entry in config.model_rate_limits. On a deployment with no per-model rate limits the family never appears while the same estimator keeps driving budget debits and the price ceiling, so the red not reported series at 1 means unmeasured rather than accurate. The family carries only the model label, so the Tenant and Credential dropdowns do not apply. Runbook: docs/operator-runbook.md.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "not reported"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "short"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
